# Python bytecode caches. Running any managed .py script (the herdr
# command-palette plugin, for example) drops a __pycache__ directory next to
# it. Without this rule a stray cache inside home/ becomes a managed file and
# shows up in every chezmoi diff. Python regenerates these on demand.
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/**

